53 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Low-code platforms allow applications to be developed using visual components such as forms, reports and workflows, with little hand-written code. This makes it quick to build standard business applications.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
54 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (When the standard low-code functionality is insufficient for a particular requirement, pro-code extensions allow developers to introduce programmable logic into the application. Zoho Creator supports this through Deluge, its scripting language, and through custom functions, which are reusable units of Deluge code that can be called within an application when required.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
55 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Extending a low-code application with custom functions means that the visual structure of the application \(forms, reports and workflows\) is retained, while specific logic is written as code in a function and used where required. The main concepts are as follows:)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
